A||N||22||bHooper||so i have a little problem with fiero lisa's car!||||8||
Z||000000||bHooper||03-17-2001||01:33 PM||||we are installing new springs on her '86 Gt, and the drivers side right front outer tie rod end doesnt want to come free!<P>the "bolt" is spinning with the nut.  it came lose a bit, but after a while, it has seized and spinning.<P>any suggestions with this?  we are trying to get her car done today, she doesn't have any other way to get around town.<P>thanks!<BR>hoop<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||8
Z||000001||northstar87||03-17-2001||01:51 PM||||Hey you two.  You better have that done!!  Here are a couple of hints.  Here is the first.  Overtighten the nut on the tie rod end.  This will seat the tapered tie rod into the hole better and you may be able to spin the nut off.  That is the first one.  The next one you have to use a pickle fork. Be really careful because it will dystroy the boot.  Put the fork inbetween the tie rod and its seat.  Apply pressure to it and then try to take the nut off.  The last thing is by using an impact.  I think I am out of ideas.  I hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||03-17-2001||02:05 PM||||go to sears or some place and get a nut splitter. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||03-17-2001||02:42 PM||||chris, the bolt spins both ways.  so unfortunately we cant tighten or losen the nut.<P>will check into the splitter.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroLisa||03-17-2001||04:22 PM||||just as a note, splitter worked, hoping the tie rod isnt too messed up though...2 springs are finished, two more to go...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||03-17-2001||06:40 PM||||dont forget to check that right rear wheel lisa, It seemed to move funny when I was tightening your lugs. Make sure you dont have a bad rear ball joint or hub bearing.||||reg||1
