Z||000007||FieroLisa||03-17-2001||10:57 PM||||FINALLY DONE! Yet another one of those tasks you plan a couple hours for and it takes up the whole day...in this case i think around 11 am till 8 pm or so. (Ha, Roger and you think I spent a lot of time at your garage!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) Monday it's time for an alignment and new outer tie rod, my car is loose as hell!<p>[This message has been edited by FieroLisa (edited 03-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||William||03-18-2001||12:27 AM||||Lisa,<BR>My car's front end is lying in peices right now and you got me thinking about slapping in some of those springs while it's apart. Since your just doing this swap, you should have a good opinion on the difference in ride quaility. I would like to here your thoughts on this after you have driven the car. What brand did you go with? Did you cut the bumpers and if so how much?<P><p>[This message has been edited by William (edited 03-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||FieroLisa||03-18-2001||10:49 AM||||William,<P>Didn't have to mess with the car at all, tires are 17 in, but the same height as stock 15s. I lowered 1.5 inch with suspension techniques springs. Nothing rubs or makes funny noises, so I'm happy.<P>I would tell you how it rides, but right now its so loose, I can't even tell. It's getting aligned tomorrow at 7:30 am so I'll have a good answer for you after that. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Formula88||03-18-2001||11:12 PM||||Congrats on getting the springs done.  I had some Fiero fun in G-boro myself this weekend.  Went to StellarCon at the Marriot downtown. When I get ready to leave, the car decides to die.  Stalled and won't start back.  A mechanic friend who happened to be there says it looks like a fuel pump, but it's definately a fuel problem. Either pump, clogged line, regulator, etc.  So, $140 towing charge later I'm back in Raleigh with a dead Fiero.  I don't mind her breaking down, but why did it have to happen the FIRST time I take her on a road trip?  <P>OK, enough whining.  Just trolling for some sympathy.  When we gonna get some pics of the new springs and wheels?  Gotta see how that looks!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
